    "body": "Reproduction attempt on a third Windows 11 machine. The crash did not occur.\n\nMachine: Intel Core i9-10980XE (36 logical CPUs), NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090. Tree: `origin/main` at `a47c7ff22` (27 commits after `7a626a7f5`; no change to `headless_gpu.rs`, `egui_app/gpu.rs`, `crates/ui/Cargo.toml` or `Cargo.lock` in that range). Binary: `camcraft_ui-32feca3141066bd1.exe` (debug, `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib --no-run`). CWD `crates/ui`. No application window was started.\n\nReadings (exit code, result):\n\n| `--test-threads` | Runs | Exit 0 | Result of each run |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 12 | 10 | 10 | 1427 passed; 0 failed; 7 ignored; 70-80 s |\n| 24 | 2 | 2 | 1427 passed; 68.7 s |\n| 6 | 1 | 1 | 1427 passed; 96.0 s |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1427 passed; 284.7 s |\n\nOther recipes, one time each:\n\n- Filter `setup_` (the group that was last in flight on bacon), 12 threads, 3 runs: 132 passed each time, exit 0.\n- The GPU tests of the default set (`adapter_probe_names_the_gpu`, `headless_run_succeeds`), 12 threads, `CAMCRAFT_REQUIRE_GPU=1`, 20 runs: all exit 0.\n- The Windows event log (Application, event 1000) has no crash record of a `camcraft_ui` binary on this machine.\n\nFinding: on this machine the crash does not occur at 12 threads. The two machines that crash (bacon: Intel iGPU; lenny) have a different GPU and driver. The crash can depend on the adapter or the driver. I did not change code, because I cannot see the fault here.\n\nNext step (recommendation): run the same binary on bacon with a crash dump (WER `LocalDumps` for `camcraft_ui-*.exe`, or `procdump -e -ma`). The dump names the faulting module. If the module is a graphics driver DLL, the fix is one shared, lazily created device in `headless_gpu`. If it is not, the dump shows the resource.\n\nRelease: I remove `claimed`. No branch with work was pushed.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
